WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.805
Week 30: Por, Para, Passive, and Impersonal Se. explain purpose and cause describe processes report institutional action

2
00:00:08.805 --> 00:00:16.415
Cultural lens. Institutional notices, journalism, and when Spanish favors se over an explicit passive.

3
00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:28.507
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:28.507 --> 00:00:40.301
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:40.301 --> 00:00:49.343
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:49.343 --> 00:01:17.863
Model language. La medida fue aprobada por el consejo. — The measure was approved by the council. Se publicaron los resultados ayer. — The results were published yesterday. Trabajamos para mejorar el acceso. — We work to improve access. El servicio cerró por falta de fondos. — The service closed because of a lack of funding. Se requiere identificación para entrar. — Identification is required to enter.

7
00:01:17.863 --> 00:01:27.761
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
